The Tourism and Hospitality Industry is one of the economic pillars of the Maltese economy. It is therefore crucial to ensure that the adequate people are employed and that their skills and abilities are enhanced and developed overtime so as to ensure that the best quality service is delivered. These results are mainly achieved by ensuring that the adequate Human Resources Management Systems are in place all throughout the sector.
The aim of this module is to review the role and implications of the different measures of human resource management systems that may be applied in the hospitality sector.
